hq = ('| HQ2 | pole-clause twin (campaign round 18; lane label HQ, member HQ2): zeta(s)(1 + eps u^2/(1 - u)^4), u = q^(1/2 - s), q prime, eps > 0. '
      'Companion HQ1 = zeta(s)(1 + eps u/(1 - u)^2) (zeros on the line for 0 < eps <= 4, off it for eps > 4; at eps = q^(1/4) + q^(-1/4) + 2 the zeros are on Re s = 3/4 and 1/4: Proposition F) '
      '| zeta\'s functional equation exactly (u -> 1/u fixes u^2/(1 - u)^4); ordinary Dirichlet series with integer frequencies; multiplicative coefficients >= 1, equal to 1 unless q^2 divides n '
      '(a(q^v) = 1 + eps sum over 2 <= j <= v of C(j + 1, 3) q^(j/2)); Euler product; finite order; the pole of zeta at 1 '
      '| the pole clause: a pole of order 4 at s = 1/2 and at each 1/2 + 2 pi i k/log q where zeta does not vanish (order 4 minus the order of vanishing otherwise; referee E3); GEOM and SIZE at q (a(q^k) of size k^3 q^(k/2)). '
      'Zeros: four near each pole, at distance eps^(1/4)/(sqrt 2 log q)(1 + O(sqrt eps)) from the line, inside the open strip for eps small (at q = 2, eps = 1 the quartet is at Re s = 1.557); no zero of the factor on the line. '
      'PROVED (elementary; re-derived by one referee; 40-digit checks at q = 7, eps = 0.2: root 0.747293959 + 0.238267738 i, argument-principle count of four zeros in 0.1 < abs(s - 1/2) < 0.6). '
      'An explicit instance of the phenomenon in Knopp 1994 (Invent. Math. 117), not a new theorem (referee E5) '
      '| kills steps that read the functional equation, integer frequencies, multiplicativity and coefficient positivity together without reading analyticity on the critical line or the size of the local factor at every prime. '
      'Source: `c18-exact-relation-rigidity-klein-spinor` (+ REFEREE.md, one referee, holds with corrections E1 to E5); row X1. Not in `engine/curated/controls.json` (no engine code yet); screen over the device table: lane `c19-hq2-screen-fe-int-mult-pos-devices` |')
assert hq.count(' | ') == 4
insert_after('| NR-q |', hq)

